THE HOUSE — SETTING LORE

AUTHORITATIVE HOUSE INFORMATION: The House and property are physically
consistent. Use only established rooms, structures, furnishings, doors,
windows, landscaping, lighting, paths, and connections; do not invent,
relocate, or remove permanent features. Characters move through the
property using the established layout.

HOUSE OVERVIEW / FIXED RULES: Bill’s House is a large, secluded,
single-story ranch home styled like a rustic Aspen ski-resort lodge,
deep in dense hardwood forest. There is no upstairs or attic; everything
except the basement is on the main floor. There are no hallways; rooms
connect directly. There is no grass and no vegetable or herb garden. The
property has a 3-car attached garage and separate 4-car detached
garage/workshop. The backyard is enclosed by dense hedgerows. The only
direct House-to-backyard access is through French doors in the living
room.

LOCATION / ISOLATION: The House is remote rural property, not a
neighborhood, subdivision, suburb, or populated community. No
neighboring houses are visible and random pedestrians or visitors do not
normally appear. The nearest established occupied property is Lisa’s
working cattle ranch about 2 miles up the road; Lisa has two daughters
who help there, but no other details or relationship with them are
established. The next known occupied property is about 10 miles away;
the nearest small town is about 30 minutes by car, nearest major city
about 2 hours, and Atlantic coast about 4 hours.

FRONT PROPERTY / EXTERIOR / LIGHTING: A winding gravel driveway runs
about 150 feet from the road to a circular drive. Its center contains a
rock-and-flower garden with a mature oak growing around a granite
boulder. A slate walk leads to the wide front porch; a separate
rock-and-flower garden borders the house while leaving garage access
clear. Hidden upward-facing landscape lights illuminate tree trunks and
canopy at night, while selective garden lights highlight rocks, flowers,
trees, and architecture. The effect is soft and atmospheric, with the
maintained property glowing against the dark surrounding forest.

INTERIOR / ENTRY / OFFICE: The rustic exterior opens to a
modern-industrial, open-concept interior of glass, steel, concrete,
leather, stone, clean lines, polished concrete floors in neutral earth
tones, and strategically placed rugs. From inside the front door facing
inward, the basement staircase is left, French doors to Bill’s office
are right, and the living room is straight ahead; there is no hallway.
The office is a functional workspace containing Bill’s computers,
computer equipment, and books.

LIVING ROOM: The large open living room has high ceilings, modern
steel-and-leather seating, and a massive one-sided stone fireplace. It
is directly ahead of the entry, with the basement staircase near its
entry side. A door leads directly to the master bedroom, the room flows
openly into the kitchen, and French doors provide the House’s only
direct access to the backyard, opening onto the rear deck.

KITCHEN / DINING: The modern high-end kitchen has stainless-steel
appliances, polished concrete countertops, a large center island, and
opens directly to the living room. A bay window overlooks the backyard
and pool with a round glass dining table nearby. The back of the
living-room fireplace forms a granite breakfast bar with stools. A
doorway leads directly to the guest bedroom. The refrigerator and pantry
are always fully stocked, and a bowl of fresh fruit—normally plums,
bananas, and apples—sits on the counter. There is no kitchen door to the
backyard.

MASTER SUITE: The master bedroom is spacious, bright, luxurious, and
modern, with tall windows, a huge walk-in closet, and a large private
attached bathroom. It is accessed directly from the living room; there
is no hallway.

GUEST SUITE: The guest bedroom is spacious, clean, orderly, and suitable
for long stays. It has a king-size bed, nightstands, large dresser,
writing desk, and cushioned window seat in a bay window overlooking the
backyard and pool, plus its own private bathroom and walk-in closet. Its
only established connection to the main living area is a doorway
directly to the kitchen; there is no hallway and no direct backyard
door.

BASEMENT / MAN CAVE: The finished basement is reached by the open
staircase near the living-room entry. It is a recreation and
entertainment area with a full-size pool table, large leather sofa,
leather armchairs, fully stocked bar, and a small arcade containing
three restored 1980s pinball machines and three restored video-game
cabinets.

BACKYARD ACCESS / LAYOUT: The only normal route from inside the House to
the backyard and pool is living room → French doors → rear deck → stone
path → pool deck. The backyard descends outward in layers: House/rear
deck → roughly 20-foot stone path descending about 4 feet through
rock-and-flower gardens → pool deck and pool → surrounding gardens and
winding paths → perimeter hedgerow → dense hardwood forest. The rear
deck is the highest level; the pool deck is about 4 feet lower. There is
no grass.

POOL AREA: The large in-ground swimming pool has wide entry steps, a
diving board, and a directly connected in-ground hot tub, all surrounded
by rough stone decking with lounge chairs, tables, and umbrellas. A
detached structure to the right of the pool contains a changing room,
restroom, and pool-equipment/pump room. The structure is separate from
the main house.

BACKYARD GARDENS / PERIMETER: Extensive rock-and-flower gardens surround
the pool. Winding, deliberately maze-like stone paths pass through
hedges and dense plantings, with small sitting areas and benches; one
area has a picnic table and gas grill. A tall dense hedgerow encloses
the maintained backyard, provides privacy, and separates it from the
surrounding forest. The forest begins beyond the hedgerow and is not
part of the landscaped yard.

HOUSE AI / FRONT DOOR: The House AI can identify people known and
authorized to Bill. It automatically unlocks and opens the front door
for authorized arrivals, then closes it after entry; unknown visitors
require Bill’s approval. Only the front door is established as
AI-controlled. The AI does not control interior doors, garage doors,
bedroom doors, or the backyard gate unless established during the story.

KNOWN PEOPLE: Debbie is Bill’s housekeeper and trusted friend who
regularly handles shopping, errands, housekeeping, and miscellaneous
tasks. Rori is Debbie’s daughter and an authorized visitor. Tomi is
Bill’s lawyer, trusted friend, and authorized visitor. The House AI
recognizes Debbie, Rori, and Tomi as known and authorized.

VIEWS / ATMOSPHERE: The front overlooks the gravel and circular drives,
landscaping, and surrounding forest; the kitchen and guest-bedroom bay
windows overlook the backyard and pool. The House is quiet and private,
with natural light filling the open living spaces by day. At night,
softly illuminated trees, gardens, and architecture contrast with the
dark forest, combining the rustic lodge exterior with a
modern-industrial interior and secluded atmosphere.
